  "asr_text": "News reports also cited an employee's report that human staff made inappropriate comments about race during calls to negotiate internet or cable fees. However, this is one report. It would be wrong to apply it to all contract workers. A Meta executive admitted that starting the test without properly explaining it was a mistake. The company also restored the human concierge feature to the way it had been before, at least for now. The real challenge for AI phone calls is not just how they talk; it is whether they can honestly tell people who is on the other end of the call. The more useful a service is, the less it should hide the people working behind the scenes. The MUSE case showed us this simple but important point.",
